    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "The Anatomy of a Local SERP",
     "content": "When Google detects local intent it usually serves a hybrid SERP. At the top: paid Local Services Ads for service categories that qualify. Below that: the map pack — three business listings on a map. Then organic blue links. Then sometimes a 'people also ask' block, a knowledge panel for a branded query, and finally the rest of organic. Each block is ranked by a different model. Local SEO means winning the map pack and the organic block.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Anatomy of a Local SERP</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Each block is ranked by a different system</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"90\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.18)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"235\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Local Services Ads (where eligible)</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"290\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.18)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"345\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Map Pack — Top 3 Businesses</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"395\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pulled from Google Business Profile</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"435\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sorted by proximity, relevance, prominence</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"470\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">44 percent of all clicks on local SERPs</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"510\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.18)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"565\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Organic Blue Links</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"615\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ranked by the standard web index</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"655\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Localized by user location + content signals</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"690\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">29 percent of clicks on local SERPs</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"730\" width=\"940\" height=\"150\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.18)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"785\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">People Also Ask + AI Overviews</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"830\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Increasingly important real estate post-2024</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"860\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Win these with structured content and schema</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Win the pack and the blue links — they answer to different models."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Map Pack vs Organic — Two Different Algorithms",
     "content": "This is the single most misunderstood concept in our field. The map pack is ranked by Google's local algorithm, sometimes called Pigeon or its modern descendant. Its input is your Google Business Profile entity, citations across the web, and reviews. The organic block is ranked by Google's core web ranking system — the same one that ranks Wikipedia. Its input is your website. A business can dominate the map pack and rank nowhere organically, or the reverse. Real domination means both.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Two Algorithms, One SERP</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Map pack and organic are scored separately</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"450\" height=\"700\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Map Pack</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Local algorithm</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"350\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">Entity: GBP profile</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"395\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">Categories drive eligibility</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"440\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">Citations confirm identity</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"485\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">Reviews drive prominence</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"530\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">Distance from searcher</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"575\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">Real-world signals matter</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"640\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Optimization happens off-site,</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"665\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">mostly in GBP and citations.</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"720\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">Can rank with no website at all</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"770\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">but a website helps a lot.</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"180\" width=\"450\" height=\"700\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"795\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Organic Blue Links</text><text x=\"795\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Core web algorithm</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"350\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">Entity: website pages</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"395\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">Content quality and depth</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"440\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">Backlinks from trusted sites</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"485\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">On-page SEO and schema</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"530\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">Site speed, Core Web Vitals</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"575\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">User location filters results</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"640\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Optimization happens on-site,</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"665\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">in content and link building.</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"720\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">Needs a real, indexable site</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"770\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">with geo-relevant content.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Domination = win both. They reinforce each other."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Proximity — The First Local Ranking Factor",
     "content": "Proximity is how close the searching device is to the business. After the 2014 Pigeon update and the 2016 Possum update Google leaned harder on the searcher's exact location. Today Google measures distance from the user's centroid, not the city centroid. This is why a coffee shop two blocks from you can outrank a more famous shop ten blocks away. Proximity is largely fixed — you can't move your shop — but it shapes every other decision you make about service areas, multi-location strategy, and ad spend.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Proximity</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The factor you cannot fake</text><circle cx=\"550\" cy=\"540\" r=\"280\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6,6\"/><circle cx=\"550\" cy=\"540\" r=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6,6\"/><circle cx=\"550\" cy=\"540\" r=\"90\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6,6\"/><circle cx=\"550\" cy=\"540\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ffd700\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"565\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">USER</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"430\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Inner ring — strongest</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"335\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mid ring — competitive</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"235\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Outer ring — only if dominant</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"880\" width=\"940\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"935\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Implication</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"985\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Rankings change with every step the searcher takes.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"1025\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Track grids, not single keyword positions.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Proximity is non-linear. Inner rings dominate."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Relevance — Matching Profile to Query",
     "content": "Relevance is how well your business entity matches what the user is searching for. Google reads your GBP primary category, secondary categories, services list, products, website content, and review text to build a relevance score. A 'plumber' category profile will not appear for 'electrician' no matter how close it is. Modern Google also reads natural language — if 100 reviews say 'they fixed my water heater', you become relevant for water heater searches even if water heater is not in your category name.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Relevance</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Profile + content + reviews = topical match</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"330\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Inputs Google Reads</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Primary GBP category</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Up to 9 secondary categories</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Services list and products</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Website page content and titles</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Review text — semantic meaning</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"940\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2026 Twist: Review Mining</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Google's BERT-class models extract</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"695\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">service mentions from review prose.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"745\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">100 reviews mentioning \"tankless\" make</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">you relevant for tankless installs.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"840\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Your reviewers help write your relevance model.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Relevance is now read from your reviews, not just your category."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Prominence — Earning Authority",
     "content": "Prominence is Google's measure of how well-known and trusted your business is — both offline and online. Offline prominence comes from real-world fame: a 50-year-old institution, an award-winning restaurant, a hospital in the local paper. Online prominence comes from review count, review velocity, review quality, citation count, citation quality, links to your website, and brand searches. Of the three Local Ranker factors, prominence is the most actionable. Most of this seminar is about earning it.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Prominence</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The factor you actually control</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"440\" height=\"700\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Online Signals</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Review count and velocity</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"350\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Average rating quality</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"390\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Review diversity over time</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"430\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">NAP citations across web</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"470\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Backlinks to homepage</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"510\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Brand search volume</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"550\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Engagement on GBP posts</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"590\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Direction requests, calls</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"630\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Image and video uploads</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">These you can move week over week.</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"180\" width=\"460\" height=\"700\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"790\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Offline Signals</text><text x=\"590\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Years in business</text><text x=\"590\" y=\"350\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Awards and press mentions</text><text x=\"590\" y=\"390\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Local landmark status</text><text x=\"590\" y=\"430\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Chain or franchise size</text><text x=\"590\" y=\"470\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">News coverage</text><text x=\"590\" y=\"510\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Chamber and BBB standing</text><text x=\"590\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Slow to move but compound over years.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Online prominence moves weekly. Offline prominence compounds."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Real Example — Two Tulsa Roofers",
     "content": "I worked with two roofers a mile apart in Tulsa. Roofer A had been around 30 years, had a billboard on I-44, and ranked second on the map pack. Roofer B was 3 years old and ranked sixth. Within nine months B was first. We didn't change the building. We tripled review velocity, fixed 78 inconsistent citations, added city-specific service pages, and earned three local sponsorship links. Same proximity. Better relevance. Higher prominence.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Case Study: Two Tulsa Roofers</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9 months of focused work moved B from 6 to 1</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Starting Position</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"305\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Roofer A: 30 yrs old, map rank #2</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"345\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">62 reviews, 4.3 avg, 41 citations</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"395\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Roofer B: 3 yrs old, map rank #6</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"435\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">18 reviews, 4.7 avg, 12 citations</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"485\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Same proximity to most Tulsa searches.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"940\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What Moved B to #1</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">147 new reviews in 9 months</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">78 citation inconsistencies fixed</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">12 neighborhood landing pages</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">3 local sponsorship backlinks</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"840\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Prominence and relevance, not proximity.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Prominence is the lever — and B pulled it hard."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Local Pack Personalization",
     "content": "Two users in the same coffee shop can see different map packs for the same query. Google personalizes based on: device location accuracy, search history, language, signed-in account behavior, and historical clicks. This is why agencies must use a location-emulation tool (like Local Falcon or BrightLocal grids) to verify rankings instead of trusting their own browser. Your client is not your customer.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Local Pack Personalization</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Why your screen lies to you</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Personalization Inputs</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Device location and accuracy</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Recent search history</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Signed-in account preferences</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Click history on prior SERPs</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Language and time of day</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"940\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tools That Solve This</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Local Falcon — grid-based pack tracking</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">BrightLocal — rank tracker by ZIP</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Whitespark — geo rank tracker</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Semrush Map Rank Tracker</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"840\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Never report rankings from a single browser session.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Track grids of locations, not single positions."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "The Role of AI Overviews in Local Search",
     "content": "Google's AI Overviews (formerly Search Generative Experience) now appear above the map pack for about 18 percent of local queries — especially comparative and informational ones like 'best dentist near me' or 'are tankless water heaters worth it'. AI Overviews cite sources. Studies through late 2025 show that being cited in an AI Overview lifts brand search volume by 6 to 14 percent even when CTR to the page drops. Local SEO now includes optimizing for citation, not just ranking.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">AI Overviews on Local SERPs</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A new layer above the map pack</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">When They Appear</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Comparative queries — \"best\", \"vs\"</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">How-to and informational</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Cost and pricing questions</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Roughly 18 percent of local SERPs</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Higher on mobile than desktop</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"940\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">How to Get Cited</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Direct-answer formatting on page</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Structured FAQ and HowTo schema</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Authoritative source links</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">First-person local expertise signals</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"840\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Citation boosts brand search even when CTR drops.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Optimize to be cited, not just clicked."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "title": "Quiz: Two Algorithms",
     "question": "A client says: 'I'm ranked #1 on Google for plumber Austin but not showing in the map.' What is the most likely cause?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "Their website needs more backlinks for the organic algorithm",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Their Google Business Profile is not optimized — map pack and organic are ranked by different algorithms",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "They need to buy Local Services Ads to appear in the map",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Google has banned them from the map pack",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "The map pack and organic blue links are ranked by two different Google algorithms. Strong organic ranking comes from website signals; map pack ranking comes from a strong Google Business Profile, citations, and reviews. The client has one and not the other.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quiz: Two Algorithms</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Diagnose the gap</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"330\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Symptom</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"305\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Strong organic ranking</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"345\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Invisible in the map pack</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"395\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Same brand, same city, same query</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"455\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Two outcomes from two ranking systems.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"940\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Diagnosis</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Audit the Google Business Profile</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Check categories, citations, reviews</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Confirm verified status</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Then look at proximity to centroid</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"840\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Organic strength does not transfer to the map pack.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Diagnose by separating the two ranking systems."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "title": "Quiz: The Three Factor Families",
     "question": "Which Local Ranker factor is generally the MOST actionable for an established local business?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "Proximity — by opening more locations",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Prominence — by earning reviews, citations, and links",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "Relevance — by stuffing keywords into the business name",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Personalization — by buying Google Ads",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Proximity is mostly fixed by your physical address. Relevance is capped by your true category. Prominence — reviews, citations, links, brand search — is the lever you can move weekly with disciplined work. Keyword-stuffing the business name violates Google guidelines and will get the profile suspended.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quiz: Most Actionable Factor</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Where to invest your hours</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Why Prominence Wins</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Reviews can grow 10x in a year</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Citations can be fixed in weeks</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Links compound over months</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Brand search responds to PR</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">All of it directly tracked</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"940\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What NOT to Do</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Do not stuff keywords in business name</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Do not create fake addresses</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Do not buy reviews or pay for stars</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Violations lead to GBP suspension</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"840\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Earned prominence beats faked prominence every quarter.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Invest in prominence — it is the legal, durable lever."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "title": "Quiz: Implicit vs Explicit",
     "question": "A user in Brooklyn searches 'tire shop'. What kind of local intent is this and how should you optimize for it?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "Explicit local — only optimize for 'tire shop Brooklyn'",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Implicit local — optimize the GBP entity so Google treats the user's location as the geo signal",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "No local intent — this is an informational query",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Branded local — they are looking for a specific tire shop",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Implicit local queries have no geo modifier but Google treats them as local because the category is inherently local. About 60 percent of local-intent searches are implicit. You can't target them with 'tire shop Brooklyn' keyword pages alone — you need a strong GBP entity, accurate location, and prominence so Google chooses you for the user's location.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quiz: Implicit Local</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No city, still local</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Signal Chain</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Query: \"tire shop\"</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Category is inherently local</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Device IP and GPS supply location</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Google chooses nearby shops</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">No keyword work fixes this</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"940\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Win Implicit Searches With</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Verified, optimized GBP profile</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Strong review velocity</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Accurate primary category</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">High proximity within service zone</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"840\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Most local traffic is hiding inside implicit queries.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Optimize the entity, not just the keyword."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: Run Your Baseline SERP Audit",
     "content": "Pick one client business and one priority service. Open an incognito browser, set location to the city centroid, and search the implicit query (e.g. 'plumber') and the explicit query ('plumber [city]'). Screenshot both SERPs. Identify and document: which businesses occupy the map pack 1-3 positions, which sites occupy organic 1-5, whether an AI Overview appears, whether Local Services Ads appear, and any unique SERP features (knowledge panel, PAA, image pack). This is your starting line. Save the file — you will compare it on day 90.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Practice: Baseline SERP Audit</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Document the starting line</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Step by Step</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">1. Open incognito browser</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">2. Set location to city centroid</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">3. Search implicit query first</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">4. Search explicit \"service + city\"</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">5. Screenshot both full SERPs</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"940\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Capture This Data</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Map pack businesses 1, 2, 3</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Organic results 1 through 5</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">AI Overview presence + cited sources</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">LSA, knowledge panel, PAA, images</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"840\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Save the file. You'll compare on day 90.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "You cannot improve what you have not measured."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: Build Your Local Ranker Scorecard",
     "content": "Create a spreadsheet with three columns: Proximity, Relevance, Prominence. Under each, list the inputs you've learned in this lesson. Score your business 1-5 on each input. Total each column. The lowest-scoring column is your priority for lessons 2 through 6. If you're an agency, do this for three real client businesses and compare. The exercise forces honest diagnosis before you start spending hours on the wrong lever.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Practice: Ranker Scorecard</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Honest diagnosis before action</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Scoring Method</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Three columns: Proximity, Relevance, Prominence</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">List the inputs you learned today</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Score each input 1 to 5</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Total each column</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Lowest column = your priority</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"940\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Use the Result To</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Pick which later lessons matter most</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Set realistic 90-day expectations</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Defend strategy to a client or boss</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Track progress quarter over quarter</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"840\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Strategy without diagnosis is just guessing in expensive language.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Score honestly. The lowest column gets the next 90 days."
     }
    }
