     "type": "intro",
     "title": "Local Search Has Never Stood Still",
     "content": "Everything this book has covered so far — Google Business Profile optimization, citations, reviews, content, links, technical markup, measurement — describes how to compete well within the local search system as it currently works. But that system itself has changed substantially over time, and understanding the direction of that change matters as much as mastering any single current tactic, because tactics tuned to yesterday's algorithm can quietly stop working, or even become counterproductive, as the underlying system shifts. Local search has gone through several distinct eras since the local pack (the map-plus-three-listings block shown for many local queries) became a fixture of search results. Early eras rewarded aggressive, sometimes spammy tactics — keyword-stuffed business names, dozens of thin citation-only listings, virtual offices in prime locations purely to rank — that later, named algorithm updates specifically targeted and suppressed. Google does not always name local-specific updates as prominently as its broader core algorithm updates, but several — widely referred to in the industry by informal names such as 'Possum' and 'Vicinity' — produced sharp, documented shifts in how proximity, business filtering, and duplicate-listing suppression worked, and practitioners who understood the shift early adapted faster than those who kept running old playbooks. More recently, the introduction of AI-generated summaries directly in search results, alongside the traditional local pack, has begun changing what a 'top result' even means for many local queries, since a searcher may now get a synthesized answer describing several nearby options in prose, with the local pack demoted further down the page or supplemented by generative content. This lesson traces that history briefly, then focuses on what changes are actively reshaping local search visibility right now, and how to keep a local SEO strategy resilient to a landscape that keeps moving rather than betting everything on today's exact mechanics.",
